    "field": "Ocean acidification",
    "problem": "The full severity of anthropogenic ocean acidification is difficult to assess because the unprecedented rate of CO2 emissions is projected to cause pH changes far greater and faster than the slower, naturally-buffered changes that occurred over the past 300 million years.",
    "method": "The study uses an ocean general-circulation model forced with a fossil-fuel emissions scenario to project future ocean pH, comparing these projections with past pH changes estimated using a geochemical box model and geological CO\u2082 records.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify future changes in ocean pH resulting from anthropogenic CO2 emissions and compare these changes to those estimated from the geological record of the past 300 million years.",
